  "question": "The phase difference between displacement and acceleration of a particle in a simple harmonic motion is :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\pi$ rad",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$ rad",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ rad",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "zero",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "In SHM, $a = -\\omega^2x$. The acceleration is always opposite to the displacement, so they differ in phase by $\\pi$ rad.",
